surya: keep the Vulkan device after a GPU restart (after UniXNU c72a8a5, "fix(mesa): keep the Vulkan device after
a GPU restart"). The kernel (SweetAccelerator v2, sweet_gpu.c) recovers from a hang or fault with a soft reset and
retires the submissions in flight; the device's memory, pipelines and queues stay valid. Marking the device lost made
backboardd's Metal device refuse everything afterwards (DeviceLost on every surface import) and the UI froze.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_darwin.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_darwin.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_darwin.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_darwin.cc
@@ -979,8 +979,9 @@
    if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS)
       return vk_device_set_lost(&device->vk, "error getting GPU status: 0x%x", kr);
    if (reply.faults != device->fault_count) {
+      /* The kernel ended this device's submissions in flight at a hang or a fault and restarted the GPU; memory,
+       * pipelines and queues are as they were, so only those command buffers are lost, not the device. */
       device->fault_count = reply.faults;
-      return vk_device_set_lost(&device->vk, "GPU faulted or hung");
    }
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
